# Build-time variables (read by Astro/Vite during `npm run build`). Copy to
# .env, which is gitignored. Production builds run in GitHub Actions
# (deploy.yml) with no .env, so every value here must have a safe default.

# ── Analytics consent ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Consent is REQUIRED unless this is exactly 0. Required means: nothing is
# sent until the visitor accepts the banner, and an unanswered banner counts
# as a no. The same inlined value gates the browser and the relay endpoint.
#
# This is the opposite default to alley-admin and toastbyte.studio, where
# PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_REQUIRE_CONSENT=1 turns consent on. Those are built by
# Cloudflare Pages with the variable set in the dashboard; this site isn't,
# so a missing variable has to fail closed. See isAnalyticsConsentRequired()
# in src/lib/analytics-consent.ts.
#
# Leave it unset. Set it to 0 only for local testing of the no-consent path.
# PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_REQUIRE_CONSENT=0
